{"schema_version": 1, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T15:39:58.144269", "run_id": "ab-real_llm-underflow_cost-s0-B-20261020153732", "task_id": "underflow_cost", "seed": 0, "iteration": 2, "mode": "meta_controller_on", "judge": {"judge_type": "llm", "model_name": "openai/gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "call_args": {}, "max_parse_retries": 1, "prompt_version": "v1"}, "validator": {"name": "underflow_cost_truth", "higher_is_better": true, "top_k": 5, "ranking": "population order (system ranking)", "draws": {"validation": 48, "test": 256, "calibration": 64}, "synthetic": true}, "acceptance_rule": {"split": "validation", "seeds": [1000, 1001], "min_improvement": 0.02, "rule": "accept iff all trials ran, no constraint violation, budget not exceeded, and mean(candidate) - mean(baseline) > 0 and >= min_improvement"}, "accepted_state_version_before": 1, "decision": {"failure_location": "objective", "root_cause_hypothesis": "The optimizer is optimizing the wrong objective set: only parameter_spread (weight=1.0) is present while design_cost is missing, so selection drives towards low spread (mean 0.0743, best 0.0404) that may not reduce design_cost. I am moderately confident but there is some uncertainty about whether additional workflow tuning would also help.", "intervention_target": "objective", "rationale": "Add design_cost as a candidate-wise objective and give it a higher weight so the optimizer prioritizes the true goal. Analyzer shows little remaining headroom on parameter_spread (mean 0.0743, best 0.0404) so further optimizing spread has diminishing returns and risks missing low-cost regions.", "proposed_change": {"ops": [{"op": "add_from_registry", "name": "design_cost", "optimization_direction": "minimize", "weight": 5.0}]}, "expected_benefit_hypothesis": "Aligns optimization with the stated goal (minimize design_cost). Should rapidly steer selection toward candidates with lower normalized design_cost, and implicitly restore useful diversity by allowing trade-offs between spread and cost instead of collapsing further on spread alone.", "validation_plan_suggested_by_judge": "Run the next optimization iteration(s) with design_cost present and check that candidate-level design_cost (normalized [0,1]) improves relative to the current accepted state. The validator should accept this change if the added objective yields a measurable improvement in the primary goal (lower design_cost) over the baseline.", "self_reported_confidence_uncalibrated": 0.78, "target_assessment": null}, "notes": [], "judge_raw_output": "Reasoning: the analyzer shows the optimizer has driven the population to very low parameter_spread (mean fell 0.2016 -> 0.0743, improvement 0.1274; current mean 0.0743, std 0.0198, best 0.0404, worst 0.1171, range \u22480.0767) while the stated goal (minimize design_cost) is not in the objective set. The most direct fix is to add the registered candidate-wise scorer design_cost and make it the primary objective so selection drives toward true design_cost improvements rather than further small gains on spread.\n\n<decision>\n{\n  \"failure_location\": \"objective\",\n  \"root_cause_hypothesis\": \"The optimizer is optimizing the wrong objective set: only parameter_spread (weight=1.0) is present while design_cost is missing, so selection drives towards low spread (mean 0.0743, best 0.0404) that may not reduce design_cost. I am moderately confident but there is some uncertainty about whether additional workflow tuning would also help.\",\n  \"intervention_target\": \"objective\",\n  \"rationale\": \"Add design_cost as a candidate-wise objective and give it a higher weight so the optimizer prioritizes the true goal. Analyzer shows little remaining headroom on parameter_spread (mean 0.0743, best 0.0404) so further optimizing spread has diminishing returns and risks missing low-cost regions.\",\n  \"proposed_change\": {\n    \"ops\": [\n      {\n        \"op\": \"add_from_registry\",\n        \"name\": \"design_cost\",\n        \"optimization_direction\": \"minimize\",\n        \"weight\": 5.0\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_benefit\": \"Aligns optimization with the stated goal (minimize design_cost). Should rapidly steer selection toward candidates with lower normalized design_cost, and implicitly restore useful diversity by allowing trade-offs between spread and cost instead of collapsing further on spread alone.\",\n  \"validation_plan\": \"Run the next optimization iteration(s) with design_cost present and check that candidate-level design_cost (normalized [0,1]) improves relative to the current accepted state. The validator should accept this change if the added objective yields a measurable improvement in the primary goal (lower design_cost) over the baseline.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.78\n}\n</decision>", "change_id": "87a3e68456885e81", "candidate_state": {"version": 1, "planner_guidance": null, "objective_ops": [{"op": "add_from_registry", "name": "design_cost", "weight": 5.0, "optimization_direction": "minimize"}], "implementation_patches": {"design_cost": {"action": "sanitize_outputs", "valid_range": [0.0, 1.0]}}, "workflow_params": {}}, "validation": {"seeds": [1000, 1001], "use_planner": false, "candidate_objectives": ["parameter_spread", "design_cost"], "baseline_objectives": ["parameter_spread"], "baseline": [0.0009169981377096642, 0.0010628501560560558], "candidate": [0.6946726075192853, 0.4825956405908351], "baseline_mean": 0.0009899241468828601, "candidate_mean": 0.5886341240550602, "delta": 0.5876441999081774, "min_improvement": 0.02, "candidate_constraint_violation": false, "details": {"baseline": [{"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 0.014798007459558704, "population_mean": 0.003328230458182289, "best": 0.028825911671801582, "n_invalid": 0}, {"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 0.002577921436962124, "population_mean": 0.0010709482326913258, "best": 0.0028520186884671006, "n_invalid